==Strategy==
Do not bring a Sniper powerup to this stage, as it can heavily mess with your units' attacks.

While this stage might not seem assuming without any clear secondary pusher like a Shadow Boxer K, Zeruel alone is enough to be its own pusher. Zeruel as a boss has ridiculous stats, with 2.5 million health, enough damage to kill basically everything and an Omni Strike reaching up to 900 range, meaning only the most extreme of superbackliners like [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can avoid an attack. Zeruel also has a multitude of immunities, meaning the only Cat Cannon that's worth bringing is the [[Ototo Corps#Iron Wall|Iron Wall]]. The main strategy you'll want to follow is to use Cyberpunk Cat to chip down Zeruel, making sure it doesn't have the opportunity to push at all by utilizing stallers like Metal Cat and Boulder Cat. The peons are what will make this a living nightmare, becoming more oppressive as time goes on. As you can guess, this gets very tedious very quickly.

==='''3 Crown Strategy'''===
With the tripling of magnifications comes a whole new world of insanity. On 3 Crown, every single enemy here becomes a genuine threat with horrifying stats, like a Doge Dark with 48,000 damage, a Gabriel with 156,000 health, and a Gory with 180,000 health. Because Zeruel's damage and health are now tripled, you need to make sure your Rock is boosted to 50 to prevent him from dying, as well as making sure your timings are perfectly proper in every way. Luring Zeruel is recommended to help make your timings easier. The main peons to look out are for Gabriel and Gory: a stack of Gabriels is incredibly hard to deal with given their raw stats and Area Attack, while Gory is pretty tanky and has high damage. You should also try your best to prevent Zoge burrowing at all using raw damage, because if Zoge burrows your Metal will get chipped down by the other peons, allowing Zeruel to move up and potentially blow up your Cyberstack / EVA Angel Killer Ubers / your base.

Outside of this, expect a long and arduous fight ahead of you.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Metal Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Metal Cat]]: Extremely recommended to bring along here. Its Metal attribute means that it can tank up to twelve hits from Zeruel assuming there's no other peons, allowing him to singlehandedly relieve you of the pain of having to time meatshields into Zeruel's hits.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Alongside a bunch of Research [[Cat Combo]]s, Rock is one of the best units to bring along here. With Rock's enormous healthpool, Zeruel won't be able to actually kill Rock, and it can stall out the peons for a bit too.
*[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]]: Jelly Dumpling will be one of your main units to bring along to clear out Gory and the others. A level 50 Jelly Dumpling is able to one-shot every peon here aside from Gabriel. Note that Jelly Dumpling cannot connect well onto Zeruel or Gabriel, and that a non-True Formed Slime cannot use Gory as a stepping stone.
*[[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]: Provides on-demand damage to chip down a Gory or Gabriel after Slime attacks.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]: Alongside Talents, Bahamut can easily clear waves of peons and even get some chip damage onto Zeruel. Using Bahamut to get a few hundred thousand damage onto Zeruel during its downtime is recommended in order to make this stage not take ten minutes to clear. On 3 Crown, you should save Bahamut to instantly kill the Gory.
*[[Elder Mask Doron (Special Cat)|Awakened Doron]]: One of your most important units here for higher difficulty clears. When boosted all the way to 50, Doron can tank a 300% Zeruel hit to the face and unleash a damaging Surge which can force damage knockbacks onto everything here.
*Talented [[Cats in a Box (Special Cat)|Heavy Assault C.A.T]]: C.A.T alongside Bullet Train is your main unit to knock out Doge Dark, who is arguably the strongest peon here. While C.A.T might not be too needed on 1 Crown, on 3 Crown the Doge Dark is so threatening that almost any No Uber clear will require C.A.T. Note that a Massive Damage vs. Black at any tier of B or higher can two-shot a Doge Dark on 3 Crown.
*[[Ancient Egg: N004 (Special Cat)|Supercar Cat]]: Supercar's high speed and damage makes him a strong tool to chip Zeruel's massive health pool. Note that because of his terrible range, Supercar should only be used when there are no peons on screen.
*[[Pogo Cat (Rare Cat)|Jiangshi Cat]]: On 3 Crown, a Talented Jiangshi alongside Metal and Rock will be your main staller. With its Speed talent, Jiangshi becomes a very important unit to help tank a hit.
*[[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]]: A speedy anti-Angel version of Fishman which has good enough damage to take off huge amounts of Gabriel's health. Don't use Cafeteria on anything else, as his base damage is not that great.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: A speedy generalist who can deal huge damage to the Ginger Snache, assuming he doesn't go into his blindspot.
*[[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]]: Seafarer's Survive and decent damage makes him a pretty good unit to use here as a generalist attacker for the peons. If you lure, Seafarer also has enough speed to get a hit off on Zeruel before he gets demolished by Zeruel's strike.
*EVA Angel Killers: If you managed to roll any of the Super Rares in the collab, you can simply just use them alongside You Will Find Happiness to destroy Zeruel quickly, although this becomes easier said than done on 3 Crown due to the Super Rares not being the best against the overbuffed peons.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
''Thanks to Zeruel's ridiculous stats, basically the only valid Ubers that could even stand a chance here are anything with [[EVA Angel Killer]]. At higher magnifications, even most of those will be rendered useless.''
*[[EVA Unit-00 (Uber Rare Cat)|Eva Unit-00]]: With one of the highest raw stats in the event, Eva Unit-00 can take a beating and dish out punishment for a decent period of time before being taken out.
*[[One-Eyed Asuka (Uber Rare Cat)|Blue-Eyed Asuka]]: Asuka's huge damage and Surge allows her to easily trigger Zeruel's damage knockbacks, and her piercing range also makes her very effective against the peons, who all have high knockback counts. Because of 3 Crown's ridiculous magnifications, make sure your Asuka is boosted to level 50 to prevent her from taking a damage knockback every Zeruel hit, as trying to get her to land hits when she gets constantly knockbacked is pretty hard to accomplish.
*[[EVA Unit-02 (Uber Rare Cat)|EVA Unit-02]]: EVA Unit-02's high natural stats, LD attacks and Strengthen means that it can easily tank a Zeruel hit and unleash a heavy damage hit onto the peons and Zeruel, making it one of the best options for this stage.
*[[Moonshade Kaworu (Legend Rare Cat)|Moon Disciple Kaworu]]: Good set of abilities and stats that can counter both Zeruel, and the periodic Gories.
*[[Kasa Jizo (Uber Rare Cat)|Ultra Kasa Jizo]]: Jizo's unique properties in his Ultra Form: high mobility, speed, and Survive, allows him to tear through this stage. Boasting high damage against the peons and a Survive to tank Zeruel hits, with Jizo's Ultra Form you can easily spam him to tear through Zeruel's health quickly during its downtime.

